/-
  RelSem.T4Defs — arc-7 S5a (defs half; see T4AppEq) (2026-08-20): THE T4 HARNESS APP EQUATION
  — THE EXIT-CRITERION TARGET (struct-layout points-to: member
  write/read of a symbolic v through a second member's write).

  TAG-GLOBAL BOUNDARY (honesty note): struct LAYOUT (sizeof/alignof/
  member offsets) is computed by CerbMem against the PROCESS-GLOBAL tag
  table (`CerbTags.tagDefs ()` — the native-extern state behind the
  census-pinned `with_tagDefs`/`forceIO` boundary; CerbTags.lean).
  The harness executable establishes it before running
  (Main.lean --call: `CerbTags.setTagDefsIO runFile.tagDefs`). The
  kernel cannot see through the extern, so every layout-dependent
  equation here carries the hypothesis
      htags : CerbTags.tagDefs () = t4File.tagDefs
  — EXACTLY the state Main establishes. T4's statement (RelSem/T4.lean)
  surfaces the same hypothesis; this is the tag-global's boundary
  entry exercised, not an extra axiom.

  Discovery record (SlateProbe walk of `callND t4File "memb"
  [intValue 11]`, tags set): prefix + ONE driver2 iteration with
  FIFTY-SIX dnms rounds — create struct s (R0-R2, layout htags),
  store-unspecified s (R3-R5), load v (R6-R9), member_shift .a + the
  NEG-store transform + conv chain + store s.a=v (R10-R24, exclusion
  id 0 + fresh symbol from the run-state supplies), the same cycle for
  s.b=7 (R25-R41, exclusion id 1), load s.a (R42-R49), kill (R50-R52),
  Erun conv_loaded_int (R53), final eval (R54-R55), terminal R56.
  x-sensitivity: the loads' byte roundtrips + the two conv range
  checks on x (the s.b cycle is at the literal 7).

  House rules: no sorry, no axioms, no Iris imports. Under the
  in-build audit (imported by RelSem.T4).
-/

